        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹಲ್ಲು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಲ್ಲು (hallu) — \"a tooth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian pal. Tamil kept பல்; Telugu took a third road and came out with పన్ను; Kannada applied its own law and got ಹಲ್ಲು (hallu), the p- turned to h- exactly where the chapter before said to watch for it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That makes ಹಣ್ಣು and ಹಲ್ಲು (hallu) a matched pair: two inherited words, one h apiece, and a p at the front of both a thousand years ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: a leg and a tooth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "hallu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *hallu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kālu, then hallu, and say which of the two also names a fraction",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kālu*, then *hallu*, and say which of the two also names a fraction]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
