        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕೂದಲು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೂದಲು (kūdalu) — \"hair\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೂದಲು (kūdalu) is the hair on a head, counted as a mass rather than strand by strand. Tamil's கூந்தல் (kūntal) is the same inherited word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Look at what it finishes on. ಕಾಲು (kālu), ಹಲ್ಲು (hallu), ಕಣ್ಣು and ಹಣ್ಣು all end on a small -u as well. Kannada dislikes leaving a word standing on a bare consonant and sets a light vowel behind it — a prop, carrying no meaning of its own. Tamil tolerates the bare consonant and writes பல் and கால் with nothing after them at all."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Careful Kannada also has ಕೇಶ (kēśa), straight from Sanskrit, for the barber's signboard and the poem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: a leg, a tooth, and hair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kūdalu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kūdalu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all three, and listen for the little -u at the end of each",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: all three, and listen for the little *-u* at the end of each]"
            }
          ]
        },
